        <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/149#Cali%20Willet> ;
    schema:dateCreated "2021-08-18T23:17:42Z" ;
    schema:dateModified "2026-05-13T12:52:41Z" ;
    schema:datePublished "2021-08-19T06:24:22Z" ;
    schema:description """Flashlite-Trinity contains two workflows that run Trinity on the [University of Queensland's HPC, Flashlite](https://rcc.uq.edu.au/flashlite).  Trinity performs de novo transcriptome assembly of RNA-seq data by combining three independent software modules Inchworm, Chrysalis and Butterfly to process RNA-seq reads. The algorithm can detect isoforms, handle paired-end reads, multiple insert sizes and strandedness. Users can run Flashlite-Trinity on single samples, or smaller samples requiring &lt;500Gb of memory or staged Trinity which is recommended for global assemblies with multiple sample inputs. Both implementations make use of Singularity containers to install software. 

Infrastructure\\_deployment\\_metadata: FlashLite (QRISCloud)""" ;
    schema:identifier "https://doi.org/10.48546/workflowhub.workflow.149.1" ;
    schema:isPartOf <https://workflowhub.eu/collections/6> ;
    schema:keywords "trinity, Transcriptomics, Assembly, illumina, salmon, scalable, global assemblies, rna-seq, de novo, transcriptome, strandedness, rna, singularity, container, PBS" ;
    schema:license "https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-3.0" ;
    schema:name "Flashlite-Trinity" ;
    schema:producer <https://workflowhub.eu/projects/30>,
        <https://workflowhub.eu/projects/43> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage <https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/149#shell_script> ;
    schema:sdPublisher <https://about.workflowhub.eu/> ;
    schema:url "https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/149?version=1" ;
