<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/1748?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow,
        schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
    dcterms:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE/> ;
    schema:contributor <https://workflowhub.eu/people/575> ;
    schema:dateCreated "2025-06-24T10:19:49Z" ;
    schema:dateModified "2025-06-24T10:19:49Z" ;
    schema:description """Image processing from movies to micrographs, including CTF estimation and quality filters for image curation.

**Adapting to Tilted Samples**

To process tilted experiments, use ”tilted” templates. These are modified workflows tailored to handle high drift and lower resolution commonly observed in tilted samples. Key adjustments include:

* **Motion Correction Filters**: Max per-frame shift = 30; Global drift = 120.


* **CTF Consensus Filters**: Adapted to 6.5 Å and 8.5 Å resolution cutoffs.


* **Defocus Sampler**: Trains with 500 images to select 25 diverse examples, ensuring a generalizable picking model.
""" ;
    schema:image "https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/3421/diagram?version=1" ;
