<https://workflowhub.eu/workflows/2030?version=1> a ns1:ComputationalWorkflow,
        schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
    dcterms:conformsTo <https://bioschemas.org/profiles/ComputationalWorkflow/1.0-RELEASE/> ;
    schema:contributor <https://workflowhub.eu/people/1045> ;
    schema:creativeWorkStatus "Stable" ;
    schema:dateCreated "2025-12-10T10:59:33Z" ;
    schema:dateModified "2026-05-13T13:05:21Z" ;
    schema:description """This workflows contains a pipeline in Scipion that performs the following steps:

1) Import atomic structure: introduces a protein atomic structure in the pipeline as receptor.

2) Receptor preparation: uses bioPython to prepare the receptor structure, removing waters, adding hydrogens and removing unnecessary chains if asked. Also, uses PDBFixer to optimize the structure if selected.

3) Protein pocket search: uses 3 different software (P2Rank, AutoSite and FPocket) for predicting the receptor pockets.

4) Performs a consensus over the predicted pockets to extract those that are shared among the different programs.""" ;
